AI Mode without login

The search API answers POST /chat without a login (optional_auth; it stores the
conversation only for a logged-in user), but the frontend asks for one: the chat
page covers itself with "Authentication Required", and the AI Mode toggle on the
landing and results pages starts a login instead of turning on. Give anonymous
visitors AI Mode, and say what needs an account:

- SearchInput: the AI Mode toggle works without login; the isLoggedIn prop is
  left in place, ignored, so that the pages passing it stay unchanged.
- ChatPage: no login gate. Without login, the sidebar says that conversations are
  kept only with an account (they live in the page's run store until a reload)
  and offers the login; deleting one only drops it from the page (nothing is
  stored, and the API's DELETE /conversations needs a login); a stored
  conversation's address answered with 401 goes to a new conversation.
- ChatExportPage: exports a conversation of this visit (in the run store) without
  login too; a stored one still asks for it.

Still need an account, unchanged: the conversation history (GET /conversations,
GET /conversation/{id}), the profile with API keys, the Data Player.

Upstream's tests of the gate (SearchInput.test.tsx, ChatPage.test.tsx,
ChatExportPage.test.tsx) are not changed; our image build does not run them.

Applies to matchmaker v0.14.0 (e7138c898926ebb79e45dd7d20cbf838dcf5dbe5).

